# Resource licenses

This repository distributes source code, configuration and synthetic test fixtures.
It does not distribute downloaded genomic files, publication text or measured analysis outputs.
The scripts retrieve resources whose licenses remain separate from the code license.

| Resource | Attribution and license record |
|---|---|
| ChEMBL | ChEMBL uses CC BY-SA 3.0. Preserve its attribution and share-alike terms for derived data. https://chembl.gitbook.io/chembl-interface-documentation/about |
| Open Targets | Cite the Open Targets Platform and preserve the license of each contributing source. https://platform.opentargets.org |
| Reactome | Cite Reactome and retain its source license. https://reactome.org/about/license-agreement |
| PubTator3 | Cite PubTator3. Retrieved publication text retains the publisher's license. https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/pubtator3/ |
| STRING | Cite STRING and retain the applicable release license. https://string-db.org |
| Human Phenotype Ontology | Retain the license supplied with the downloaded HPO release. https://github.com/obophenotype/human-phenotype-ontology |
| GIAB and ClinVar | Retain the attribution supplied with each downloaded benchmark or annotation release. https://www.nist.gov/programs-projects/genome-bottle and https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/clinvar/ |

The resource manifest records release identifiers and checksums where the runner requires pinned inputs.
